{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Staff of bread.</b> A term of support, as in ״מַטֵּה עֹז״ (Jeremiah 48)." "<b>When I break for you the staff of bread.</b> I will break for you every support of food — and they are the arrows of famine (Ezekiel 5)." "<b>And ten women shall bake your bread in one oven.</b> From lack of wood (Sifra)." "<b>And they shall return your bread by weight.</b> That the grain rots and becomes crumbling bread, and it breaks in the oven, and they sit and weigh the fragments to divide them among themselves (there)." "<b>And you shall eat and not be satisfied.</b> This is a curse within the intestines in the bread. Behold seven punishments: sword, siege, pestilence, breaking of the staff of bread, lack of wood, crumbling bread, curse in the intestines. And ״וְנִתַּתֶּם״ is not counted among them — it is the sword."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:46.242438725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}